---
import '../design/design-aids.css';
import SketchSheet from '../design/SketchSheet.astro';
import SketchArrow from '../design/SketchArrow.astro';
---
<figure class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface concurrent-decision" aria-labelledby="concurrent-decision-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · Where does the decision happen?</span>
  <h3 id="concurrent-decision-title">Waiting only helps if the decision can change</h3>
  <p>Requests A and B each want the same one remaining P7 mug. Both would record a purchase and change its available stock from 1 to 0. A reaches the write first; follow what B does while A finishes.</p>
  <section><h4>Unsafe: decide from an ordinary read</h4><div class="route"><SketchSheet tone="amber"><p>B reads <strong>1</strong></p><small>Plans to write 0</small></SketchSheet><SketchArrow /><SketchSheet><p>B’s write waits for A</p><small>A commits stock 0</small></SketchSheet><SketchArrow /><SketchSheet tone="amber"><p>B writes its planned <strong>0</strong></p><small>Still creates an order</small></SketchSheet></div></section>
  <section><h4>Coordinated: lock before deciding</h4><div class="route"><SketchSheet><p>B’s locking read waits</p><small>A holds the row lock</small></SketchSheet><SketchArrow /><SketchSheet><p>A commits; B reads <strong>0</strong></p><small>B now holds the row lock</small></SketchSheet><SketchArrow /><SketchSheet tone="teal"><p>B declines the purchase</p><small>No stock, no order</small></SketchSheet></div></section>
  <figcaption>Both attempts encounter a lock. In the first, waiting delays an already-chosen write. In the second, the protected read supplies the value used to decide. This is PostgreSQL Read Committed behaviour for the single stock row shown.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  section { margin:1.5rem 0; }
  section + section { border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule); padding-top:1.2rem; }
  .route { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 2.2rem minmax(0,1fr) 2.2rem minmax(0,1fr); align-items:center; gap:.25rem; }
  .route p { margin:0 0 .5rem; }
  small { display:block; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  @media(max-width:600px) { .route { grid-template-columns:1fr; max-width:21rem; margin:auto; gap:.5rem; } .route > :global(svg) { width:2.7rem; transform:rotate(90deg); margin:auto; } }
</style>
